From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand-build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:10:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 305/310] Spatiand: a page visited on one machine is a visited
 link on the others

Visits taken in from the other machines (HistorySync, patch 0009) were in the
history page and never coloured as visited: Chromium colours a link by its
row in the VisitedLinkDatabase (link, top-level page, frame) and the table
made from it, which only a navigation on this machine made. Now each visit
written for the others carries the page its link was followed on when
Chromium knows it ("top" and "frame", optional: older files and builds read
and write as before); a visit taken in gets its row and its place in the
table at once, under the page that came with it, or, with none (every visit
shared until now), on its own site; and what was in history before this gets
the same once (a marker in the profile's local folder,
visited-links-made).
